    "title": "Why is Friday the 13th considered unlucky?",
    "text": "March 13, 2026, 10:44 a.m. ETCross your fingers and knock on wood: Friday the 13th is upon us yet again.March 13 marks the second of three Fridays the 13th of 2026. For the superstitious, the date can feel especially unsettling – and the classic \"Friday the 13th\" slasher movie franchise probably hasn't helped ease any fears.For ages, many Western cultures have considered the number 13 itself to be unlucky. Many hotels, hospitals, and other high-rise buildings do not have a 13th floor for this reason.The unlucky date has long been a staple of pop culture and in the past even some businesses have embraced the date as a focal point for special deals.But how did Friday the 13th become associated with bad luck?Why is Friday the 13th considered unlucky?The unlucky association with Friday the 13th is likely rooted in Christianity, according to History.com. In the Bible, during the Last Supper of Jesus, 13 people were seated at the dinner table. The next day, on a Friday, Jesus was crucified.\"So 13 is associated with that terrible event. And Friday the 13th, you get a double whammy. You get both of these elements coming together: the taboo against 13, and the crucifixion, which was on a Friday,\" Dr. Phil Stevens, author and retired anthropology professor, said in a 2023 interview with USA TODAY.For ages, many Western cultures have considered the number 13 itself to be unlucky. Many hotels, hospitals, and other high-rise buildings do not have a 13th floor for this reason.Some argue the number is considered unlucky because it follows 12, which many associate with \"completeness,\" History.com said. Take the 12 days of Christmas, 12 months of the year, 12 zodiac signs, 12 labors of Hercules, 12 gods of Olympus, and 12 tribes of Israel, for example.Also, according to ancient Norse lore, evil and turmoil were brought to the world by the mischievous god Loki, the 13th guest at a dinner party in Valhalla. Legend has it that he upset the balance of the 12 gods already there, according to History.com.Friday the 13th to occur 3 times in 2026Friday the 13th occurs three times in 2026 – in February, March, and November. The last year with three instances of Friday the 13th was 2015, and the next will be 2037.Here's when the next several Friday the 13th instances will occur:Friday, Nov. 13, 2026Friday, Aug. 13, 2027Friday, Oct. 13, 2028Friday, April 13, 2029Friday, July 13, 2029Friday, Sept. 13, 2030Friday, Dec. 13, 2030Six out of 14 years have one Friday the 13th, six out of 14 years have two Fridays the 13th, and two out of 14 years have three Fridays the 13th, according to The Old Farmer's Almanac.Months that contain a Friday the 13th begin on a Sunday, the almanac said.Michelle Del Rey of USA TODAY contributed to this report.",
